IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpula-practice`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA), ss 6, 7, 20, 113, 114, 116-118, 276, 278, 279, 289, 322 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_legal-profession-uniform-law-application-act-2022.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel/facts.json): Daniel born 1996-04-09; d023 on 2019-12-10
-- ("Graduates JD; Practical Legal Training", aged 23); d031 on 2020-08-24 ("Admitted by the Supreme Court; a practising
-- certificate", aged 24); d038 on 2029-03-04 (acts in an arbitration under a conditional costs agreement with a 25% uplift, aged
-- 32). The scenario gives no date for completing practical legal training; the fixtures take the d023 date. Renewal periods,
-- determination dates and amounts below are HYPOTHETICAL inputs (the Act leaves them to regulations or to the Committee).

§ `Fixtures`

`Daniel's admission application` MEANS `Admission application` WITH
    `made in accordance with the local regulations` IS TRUE
    `made in accordance with the rules of court` IS TRUE
    `made in accordance with a practice direction` IS TRUE
    `a fee is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee is paid` IS TRUE

`an application without the prescribed fee` MEANS `Admission application` WITH
    `made in accordance with the local regulations` IS TRUE
    `made in accordance with the rules of court` IS TRUE
    `made in accordance with a practice direction` IS TRUE
    `a fee is prescribed` IS TRUE
    `the prescribed fee is paid` IS FALSE

`an application where no fee is prescribed` MEANS `Admission application` WITH
    `made in accordance with the local regulations` IS TRUE
    `made in accordance with the rules of court` IS TRUE
    `made in accordance with a practice direction` IS TRUE
    `a fee is prescribed` IS FALSE
    `the prescribed fee is paid` IS FALSE

`a complete certificate application` MEANS `Certificate application` WITH
    `in the local approved form` IS TRUE
    `with the documents the form requires` IS TRUE
    `with any prescribed fee` IS TRUE
    `with any Guarantee Fund contribution required` IS TRUE
    `with any framework contribution required` IS TRUE

`an application without the Guarantee Fund contribution` MEANS `Certificate application` WITH
    `in the local approved form` IS TRUE
    `with the documents the form requires` IS TRUE
    `with any prescribed fee` IS TRUE
    `with any Guarantee Fund contribution required` IS FALSE
    `with any framework contribution required` IS TRUE

§ `ss 6, 7 -- the Law applies from 1 July 2022`

#ASSERT NOT `the Uniform Law applies in Western Australia on` 20191210
#ASSERT NOT `the Uniform Law applies in Western Australia on` 20200824
#ASSERT `the Uniform Law applies in Western Australia on` 20220701
#ASSERT `the Uniform Law applies in Western Australia on` 20290304

§ `s 20 -- designated local regulatory authority`

#ASSERT `the designated local regulatory authority for` `Part 2.2 (admission)` EQUALS `the Legal Practice Board`
#ASSERT `the designated local regulatory authority for` `s 82(4)` EQUALS `the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`
#ASSERT `the designated local regulatory authority for` `s 436(1)` EQUALS `the Board or the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`

§ `ss 113, 114 -- admission`

#ASSERT `the admission application meets s 113` `Daniel's admission application`
#ASSERT NOT `the admission application meets s 113` `an application without the prescribed fee`
#ASSERT `the admission application meets s 113` `an application where no fee is prescribed`

#ASSERT `the Court is properly constituted to admit` 3
#ASSERT NOT `the Court is properly constituted to admit` 1

§ `s 116 -- practising certificate application`

#ASSERT `the certificate application meets s 116` `a complete certificate application`
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate application meets s 116` `an application without the Guarantee Fund contribution`

§ `s 117 -- renewal (hypothetical periods: standard 1 April to 31 May 2029, late fee period to 30 June 2029)`

#ASSERT `the renewal application is` 20290415 20290401 20290531 20290630 EQUALS `within the standard renewal period`
#ASSERT `the renewal application is` 20290615 20290401 20290531 20290630 EQUALS `in the late fee period: the Board may reject`
#ASSERT `the renewal application is` 20291001 20290401 20290531 20290630 EQUALS `late: the Board may accept only if satisfied under s 117(4)`
#ASSERT `the renewal application is` 20300105 20290401 20290531 20290630 EQUALS `the Board must reject`

#ASSERT `the 1 July immediately following` 20290630 EQUALS 20290701
#ASSERT `the 1 July immediately following` 20290815 EQUALS 20300701

§ `s 118(3) -- deemed refusal`

#ASSERT `the Board is taken to have refused` 20290601 FALSE 0 FALSE 20291202
#ASSERT NOT `the Board is taken to have refused` 20290601 FALSE 0 FALSE 20291201
#ASSERT NOT `the Board is taken to have refused` 20290601 TRUE 20290801 FALSE 20291202

§ `ss 276, 278, 279 -- admission begun under the old Act`

#ASSERT `the old application continues as a s 113 application` 20220301 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the old application continues as a s 113 application` 20220301 TRUE

#ASSERT `the old academic qualifications count under Uniform Law s 17(1)(a)` 20191210
#ASSERT NOT `the old academic qualifications count under Uniform Law s 17(1)(a)` 20221210

#ASSERT `s 279 carries the old PLT into Uniform Law s 17(1)(b)` TRUE 20191210
#ASSERT `s 279 carries the old PLT into Uniform Law s 17(1)(b)` TRUE 20230615
#ASSERT NOT `s 279 carries the old PLT into Uniform Law s 17(1)(b)` TRUE 20230701

